quran[19]{c,v,t}:
  15,52,when they entered upon him and greeted (him with): ‘Peace!’ He (Ibrahim) said: ‘We are indeed afraid of you.’
  15,53,"They (the angels) said: ‘Do not be afraid. Indeed, we give you glad tidings of a knowledgeable son.’"
  15,54,He (Ibrahim) said: ‘Do you bring me glad tidings when old age has already overtaken me? So what glad tidings have you brought me?’
  15,55,"They said: ‘We have brought you glad tidings in truth, so do not be among the despairing.’"
  15,56,"He (Ibrahim) said: ‘Who despairs of his Lord’s mercy, except those who are astray?’"
  15,57,"He (Ibrahim) said: ‘Then what is your (next) mission, O messengers?’"
  15,58,They said: ‘We have been sent to a guilty people.
  15,59,"(They shall perish) except the family of Lut (Lot). We will indeed save them all,"
  15,60,"except his wife; we have ordained, she will indeed be among those who remain behind (to perish).’"
  15,61,"So when the messengers came to Lut’s family,"
  15,62,"he (Lut) said: ‘Indeed, you are an unfamiliar people.’"
  15,63,"They said: ‘Rather, we have come to you with (the punishment) that they used to doubt."
  15,64,"And we have come to you with (the judgement of) truth, and surely, we are truthful."
  15,65,"Set out with your family (and followers) during the darkness of the night, and you should follow behind them, and none of you should turn around. And keep proceeding as you are commanded.’"
  15,66,"We decreed this command to him, that these (people of Sodom and Gomorrah) shall be uprooted by the morning."
  15,67,And the people of the town came (to Lut’s house) rejoicing.
  15,68,"He said: ‘Surely, these are my guests, so do not embarrass me (regarding them)."
  15,69,And fear (the wrath of) Allah and do not shame me.’
  15,70,"They said: ‘(O Lut,) did we not forbid you from (protecting) all the people?’"
